.TH IBUS-ENGINE-RUSTYPE 1 "November 2026" "Rustype 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ibus-engine-rustype \- Lightweight, privacy-focused Vietnamese input method engine for IBus
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ibus-engine-rustype
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ibus-engine-rustype
is a modern, high-performance, and lightweight Vietnamese input method engine designed for the IBus input method framework on Linux. It is implemented in pure Rust without external library dependencies, maintaining a minimal memory footprint (~2.5 MB RAM) and instant keystroke processing.
.PP
The engine communicates directly with the IBus daemon via standard D-Bus IPC over a local Unix domain socket. It supports both Telex and VNI input methods, modern and traditional Vietnamese orthography, automatic English word restoration, per-application input state persistence, macros (abbreviations), and intelligent application-specific composition modes (such as terminal preedit mode and surrounding text direct composition).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-doctor
Run comprehensive system diagnostic checks. Inspects the IBus daemon, component registration, GNOME input sources, display server (Wayland/X11), GNOME Shell extension, and configuration files. Outputs actionable recommendations for troubleshooting.
.TP
.B \-\-xml
Generate and print the IBus component XML specification to standard output. This XML describes the engine identity, icon, rank, and capabilities to IBus.
.TP
.B \-\-write\-config
Ensure default configuration files exist in \fI~/.config/rustype/config\fR. If the configuration file is missing, a documented default configuration is generated.
.TP
.B \-v\fR, \fB\-\-version
Print the software version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h\fR, \fB\-\-help
Display command-line help information and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUSTYPE_DEBUG
When set (e.g. \fBRUSTYPE_DEBUG=1\fR), enables safe diagnostic logging to standard error. In accordance with Rustype's privacy commitment, debug output only records hardware key codes and input states, never user keystroke text or committed content.
.TP
.B RUSTYPE_LOG
Specifies an optional file path to redirect diagnostic logs when running as an IBus subprocess.
.TP
.B IBUS_ADDRESS
Specifies the D-Bus socket address for the IBus daemon. When not set, Rustype automatically discovers the active IBus socket from \fI~/.cache/ibus/dbus-*\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/rustype/config
Main configuration file. Controls the default input method (Telex or VNI), display mode, orthography, English word restoration, macro enablement, and per-application custom modes.
.TP
.I ~/.config/rustype/macro
Macro file containing abbreviation mappings (one pair per line: \fIabbreviation:expansion\fR). Compatible with standard Unikey macro files.
.TP
.I ~/.config/rustype/words
Custom list of English words that should never be converted into Vietnamese tone marks.
.TP
.I /usr/share/ibus/component/rustype.xml
System IBus component registration file.
.SH PRIVACY & SECURITY
Rustype is engineered with an absolute commitment to user privacy:
.IP \(bu 2
\fB100% Offline:\fR The engine contains zero networking code or socket capabilities. It cannot establish outgoing or incoming network connections.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBZero Keylogging:\fR Keystrokes are processed strictly in volatile memory during word formation and immediately discarded upon commit. No keystrokes are written to disk.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPassword Field Protection:\fR Keystroke interception is completely bypassed when an input field reports the password purpose (\fIIBUS_INPUT_PURPOSE_PASSWORD\fR).
